## DO
- Place each part so its bounding box CENTRE and EXTENTS equal the plan row.
- Build what the description says at its numbers and counts: the judge's checklist marks a
  named feature that is not there (a scaled cube where the plan says "fluted cylindrical body with
  6 flutes").
- Material per part with the stated colour, roughness and metalness.
- Instances (`{{ '{' }}Name{{ '}' }}_0 … _N-1`) are built inside YOUR file, each TOP-LEVEL.

## DON'T
- Do not build, rename, move or "fix" a part that is not in your table — even if it looks wrong.
- Do not write the entry file, a README, notes or tests.
- No placeholders ("TODO", "simplified"), no unit-cube stand-ins, no part off its plan bbox by more
  than the contract tolerance (max(1 cm, 10 %) per axis).
- No environment sniffing, no DOM/texture loading/network/file IO, no camera/light/render/export.

